  m_Name: LungsInfo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OrganInfoData
  organName: Lungs
  overview: The lungs are a pair of spongy, air-filled organs located on either side
    of the chest that are responsible for respiration.
  structure: "\u2022\tLobes (Right has 3, Left has 2)\r\n\u2022\tBronchi and bronchioles\r\n\u2022\tAlveoli"
  organFunction: "\u2022\tFacilitates gas exchange\r\n\u2022\tOxygenates blood and
    removes carbon dioxide"
  didYouKnow: If you flattened out all the alveoli in your lungs, they would cover
    an area roughly the size of a tennis court.
